            B.q("ai-m3-9", "ai-container-apps", "What fits best on Container Apps?", listOf("A container app with an Azure Queue scale rule that scales to zero when idle", "A container app with an HTTP scale rule and one replica that is always running", "A Container Apps job with a schedule trigger that runs every hour on the queue", "A Container Apps job with an event trigger and a KEDA scale rule on the queue"), setOf(3), "Container Apps jobs run containers that start, do one task and exit. A job's trigger is manual, schedule (cron) or event. An event-driven job starts executions as messages arrive, which suits long tasks better than an app whose replicas can be stopped when it scales in.",
