            B.q("ai-m3-15", "ai-cosmos-sdk", "At start-up the API calls database.create_container_if_not_exists and gets 403 Forbidden, yet reads and writes of items work. What is the right fix?", listOf("Create the container through Azure Resource Manager, such as az CLI or Bicep, and only open it in code", "Assign Cosmos DB Built-in Data Contributor again, this time at account scope instead of database scope", "Give the identity the Cosmos DB Account Reader Role so that the SDK can manage containers too", "Call create_database_if_not_exists first, so that the new container has a parent database"), setOf(0), "Cosmos DB data-plane roles cover items and queries. Creating databases and containers is a control-plane operation, so with Entra ID you create them through Azure Resource Manager (CLI, Bicep, portal) and the app just opens them with get_container_client.",
