            B.q("ai-m3-17", "ai-cosmos-perf", "Total throughput is far from used, yet many requests get 429 Too Many Requests. Metrics show one partition taking almost all requests. What is the root cause and fix?", listOf("Session consistency lets replicas diverge under load; switch the account to Strong consistency", "/country is a hot key; change the existing container's partition key to /deviceId in place", "/country is a hot key; move the data to a new container with a high-cardinality key such as /deviceId", "Total throughput is too low; raise the container's RU/s with autoscale until the 429 errors stop"), setOf(2), "Throughput is divided between physical partitions. If one partition key value gets most of the traffic, that partition hits its share of RU/s and throttles even while the total is underused. A key with many evenly used values spreads the load; the partition key cannot be changed in place, so data moves to a new container.",
                scenario = "Harbor Pets partitions its telemetry container by /country, and 90 percent of its users are in one country.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
