            B.q("ai-m3-21", "ai-cosmos-vector", "In a test container with 300 items, vector queries cost far more RUs than expected, even though a diskANN index is defined. Why?", listOf("diskANN is used only under Strong consistency; with Session the query scans every item", "The container needs a flat index first, and diskANN is added once flat is populated", "Quantized indexes need at least 1,000 vectors; below that the query falls back to a full scan", "diskANN only indexes vectors of up to 505 dimensions; larger ones fall back to a full scan"), setOf(2), "The quantization that quantizedFlat and diskANN use needs at least 1,000 vectors to be accurate. Until then Cosmos DB falls back to a full scan, so RU charges are higher. Test cost with a realistic amount of data.",
