            B.q("ai-m3-24", "ai-postgres", "The API caches one Entra access token at start-up and uses it as the password for every new connection. After some hours, new connections fail to authenticate while old ones keep working. What is the fix?", listOf("Keep the server admin password in an environment variable as a fallback when sign-in fails", "Raise the pool's max_lifetime so that existing connections are recycled less often", "Restart the container every hour so that a fresh token is cached at start-up", "Get a token from DefaultAzureCredential each time the pool opens a new connection"), setOf(3), "Entra access tokens expire. A token is only checked when a connection signs in, so open connections keep working, but new ones need a current token. Calling get_token when each connection opens, for example in the pool's connection factory (the credential caches and renews tokens), fixes it.",
