            B.q("ai-m3-25", "ai-postgres", "The ride history query is WHERE user_id = %s ORDER BY started_at DESC LIMIT 20, and it does a sequential scan. Which index serves both the filter and the sort?", listOf("CREATE INDEX ON rides (started_at DESC, user_id)", "CREATE INDEX ON rides (user_id, started_at DESC)", "Two separate indexes, one on user_id and one on started_at", "CREATE INDEX ON rides USING GIN (user_id)"), setOf(1), "In a composite B-tree, put the equality column first and the sort column second. The index then jumps to one user's rows, which are already in started_at order, and LIMIT 20 stops after 20 entries.",
