            B.q("ai-m3-26", "ai-postgres", "Users want to search ride reviews by words, so a search for 'flat tyre' also finds 'flat tyres'. Which approach fits PostgreSQL?", listOf("A tsvector column of the review text with a GIN index, queried with websearch_to_tsquery", "A B-tree index on lower(review), queried with WHERE lower(review) = 'flat tyre'", "A jsonb array of each review's words with a GIN index, queried with the @> operator", "A hash index on the review column, queried with WHERE review LIKE 'flat tyre%'"), setOf(0), "PostgreSQL full-text search turns text into a tsvector of normalised words (so tyre and tyres match), and a GIN index makes searching it fast. The tsvector can be a stored generated column. websearch_to_tsquery parses search-box style input.",
