            B.q("ai-m3-57", "ai-opentelemetry", "Support staff want every log line from the API to be linked to the trace of the request that wrote it. What gives you that?", listOf("Writing log lines with print(), which the distro captures from stdout with the span's ids", "Putting the request URL and a timestamp in every log message so lines can be matched up", "Sending logs to a separate Application Insights resource kept just for log data", "Logging through a standard logging logger that the distro collects, tied to the active span"), setOf(3), "The distro connects Python's standard logging module to OpenTelemetry. A record written while a span is active gets that span's trace id and span id, which Application Insights stores as the operation id in the traces table, so you can jump from a request to its log lines.",
